# ==============================================================================
# LITERT ANDROID API LEVEL OWNERS & GOVERNANCE
# ==============================================================================
# This file governs modifications to minimum Android SDK level (minSdkVersion)
# and Android NDK API level (--android_ndk_min_sdk_version) for the LiteRT
# Android API.
#
# IMPACTS OF INCREASING API LEVELS:
# 1. Android Min SDK (minSdkVersion / minSdk):
#    - Increasing minSdkVersion drops support for older Android OS releases
#      (e.g., API 23 = Android 6.0; API 26 = Android 8.0; API 31 = Android 12).
#    - Consumer Android apps targeting older SDKs will fail to build or install
#      if LiteRT requires a higher SDK level than the app.
# 2. Android NDK API Level (--android_ndk_min_sdk_version / __ANDROID_API__):
#    - Determines system library symbol availability (libc, libm, linker APIs)
#      in compiled native shared libraries (.so) and binaries.
#    - Binaries built with a higher NDK API level will fail at runtime on older
#      devices with UnsatisfiedLinkError or symbol resolution errors.
#
# CRITERIA FOR APPROVING API LEVEL INCREASES:
# - Must be approved by designated LiteRT Android API owners.
# - Clear technical necessity (platform features that cannot be probed at runtime).
# - Impact assessment on downstream consumers (Google Play services,
#   Android OS, Tensor, MediaTek, Qualcomm, external AAR/Maven developers).
# - Consistent alignment across AndroidManifest.xml and release build scripts.
# ==============================================================================

